            <ArticleTitle>[Improvement of coronary prognosis by reducing LDL-cholesterol].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Elevated LDL-cholesterol levels mean increased risk for coronary heart disease. In different studies the indication for decreasing high LDL-cholesterol in patients with coronary heart disease was proven. This is also the case with patients suffering from high LDL-cholesterol but not yet coronary heart disease. It is supposed that with longer duration of studies the total mortality between verum and placebo groups will also reach significance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
